lete might be soft-delete (moved to trash) — still fine.\n\nActually, simpler: In the task editor for a new task, after setting the custom repeat, the repeat row shows a summary like \"Repeats weekly on Monday\" before saving. Yes! The editor shows the repeat summary text (e.g., \"Repeats monthly\"). So I can set custom repeat and see the summary, then cancel. That avoids saving.\n\nLet me do this on a new task or on Pay rent (restore after). Better use Pay rent: I'll open Pay rent, open repeat picker, choose Custom, weekly, select a specific day (e.g., Monday chip), OK, and observe the repeat row summary. Then reopen and restore to \"Every month\" (original), then back out without saving. This avoids creating data.\n\nWait, but if the mapping is off, the summary will reveal it: selecting the chip labeled \"M\" (second chip) should yield \"Repeats weekly on Monday\". Let me test.\n\nActually, currently Pay rent is monthly; changing to weekly and reading summary then restoring to monthly is safe as long as I don't save. Let me do it.\n\nFirst, from list (grouping None, sorting desc). Open Pay rent."}
