rrect.\n\nWhat about a task due on a date and then \"Custom weekly\" with a *different* weekday? We tested selecting Monday on Pay rent (due Friday Dec 4) → summary \"Repeats weekly on Mon\". If saved, would the next due be Monday? Probably.\n\nHmm.\n\nLet me look at the \"Repeats from: due date/completion date\" toggle. When set to completion date, completing the task should schedule from completion date. That's standard. Could be buggy but not in change note.\n\nMaybe the intended bug is in the *repeat picker's weekday order* in a way I haven't noticed: perhaps the **weekday chips order is Sunday-first on this locale, but the *task due date's weekday* is auto-selected based on a hardcoded Monday-first index**, causing the wrong day highlighted. When we opened custom weekly for Pay rent (due Friday Dec 4), no chips were selected initially. Hmm, that itself might be a bug: when converting from monthly to weekly, no day is selected; but if you just choose \"Every week\" quick option, it uses due date's weekday.\n\nWait, actually maybe when opening Custom recurrence for a *weekly* repeat, the chips should preselect the current repeat days. Let me test: Pay rent currently monthly. Set it to weekly (quick) then reopen Custom → does Friday get preselected? If not, that's a bug (custom dialog not reflecting current weekly schedule). Let me test on a scratch task again? Or Pay rent, restoring after. Let me do it on Pay rent carefully: set repeat Every week (quick) → summary \"Repeats weekly\" and repeats from due date. Then tap repeat → Custom → see if F (Friday) is selected (since due date Friday). Then cancel and restore monthly. This tests whether the custom dialog reflects existing weekly selection.\n\nActually, when I set Custom weekly earlier on Pay rent starting from monthly, no chip was selected. When I then selected M, summary became \"on Mon\". That's fine. But if the task was already weekly (quick option), the custom dialog should show the weekday. Let me test.\