after app restart. We saw persistence within session. What about after a full app restart (process death)? We can't kill the app, but we can background it and rotate. We did rotation. Maybe press HOME then open_app (foreground) might recreate. Let me test: set grouping direction to something non-default (e.g., By priority Ascending instead of fallback Descending), then HOME + open_app, then check if direction remains Ascending or resets to fallback Descending. If it resets, that's a persistence bug, possibly the injected one.\n\nActually, we can set By due date Desc (non-default fallback Asc), background/foreground, reopen sort → check. We already rotated with Desc and it persisted. Rotation usually recreates the activity, but the app process stays; settings persisted in SharedPreferences. Process death unlikely.\n\nHOME + open_app might not kill. Hmm.\n\nLet me think about SharedPreferences: settings are persisted to disk; process death wouldn't matter. So no.\n\nOK. Let me go back to the main screen and do a final sweep of repeating tasks: test editing Pay rent's due date and repeat \"Repeats from\" toggle, and verify the editor consistency. Actually, maybe there's a bug where the repeat picker shows \"Repeats monthly\" but the underlying repeat is on the wrong day. E.g., Pay rent due Dec 4 (Friday) but monthly repeat \"on day 4\" ✓.\n\nWait, the precondition says \"Pay rent (due in 20 days) repeating monthly\". Today Sat Nov 14 → +20 = Fri Dec 4 ✓. Good.\n\nLet me test the \"Repeats from: completion date\" option properly: toggle to completion date, save, complete Pay rent? That would alter data. Not desirable. Skip.\n\nMaybe test the repeat picker's \"Every day\" option on a scratch task to verify daily repeat next occurrence +1 day. We already verified weekly +7. Daily is similar.\n\nGiven the lack of bugs, maybe I should reconsider the *search* once more with a focus on the exact change: \"results are now refreshed as each character of the query is typed.\" Perhaps the intended behavior is that the search-as-you-type results refresh, but there's a bug where typing a character that **doesn't change the result set** triggers a refresh that **resets scroll/selection**. Not testable.\n\nOr maybe the bug is that the search results refresh per character but the **result count shown in the header** is stale. The header \"Matching 'milk'\" updates on IME search. Hmm.\n\nWhat about typing with **uppercase via shift**? type_text \"MILK\" used uppercase keys (the keyboard was uppercase after Shift? The first observation showed uppercase keys because it auto-capitalized? Actually typing \"MILK\" resulted in uppercase). Search worked.\n\nLet me test a **special character query**: \"https://example.com/guide\" or \"example.com\" or \"@\" or \"%\". If search uses SQL LIKE without escaping, \"%\" would match everything — a bug. This is a classic injected bug in search changes! Let's test: type \"%\" — if it matches all tasks, that's an unescaped wildcard bug. Also \"_\" matches any single char. This could be the injected bug in search. Let me test.\n\nGo back to main screen first."}
