{"type": "thinking", "text": "Reverted to en-US date format (\"November 24\", \"December 4\"). Good.\n\nNow, back to the decision about the wildcard search bug. Let me reconsider whether there might be a seeded bug I still haven't found. Let me perform a broader state-persistence check on search: type a query, press IME search, then rotate. Already did some.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider the \"grouping direction fallback\" with the app language now that I know the app settings. Could the fallback depend on the *sorting* direction setting that I may have altered? No.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the initial state again: grouping By due date Desc while sorting By due date Asc. If the \"new fallback\" is per-type Asc, then the initial Desc is a saved value (from seeding). Not a bug.\n\nLet me look for an off-by-one in the *weekday chips* for en-GB: we saw M T W T F S S — correct Monday-first. But are the *letters* correct? M(Mon) T(Tue) W(Wed) T(Thu) F(Fri) S(Sat) S(Sun). Yes. And the mapping? In en-US we verified chip index 1 (M) → \"Repeats weekly on Mon\" and last S → Sat. If the ordering change introduced a rotation bug only in Monday-first locales (e.g., chip 0 label M but value Sunday), we'd need to test mapping in en-GB. Hmm! That's a real possibility: the fix might reorder the labels but not the values (or vice versa). In en-US, labels start Sunday and values Sunday — consistent. In en-GB, the labels might start Monday but the values might still start Sunday, causing a mismatch.\n\nLet me test the mapping in English (UK)! I already reverted the language, though. Ugh. But this is a plausible bug: ordering by locale first day might rotate labels but not the underlying day values, so in Monday-first locales the first chip (M) might actually select Sunday. The seeded bug could be exactly that. Hmm, but the change note says weekday choices are ordered by locale first day — the expected fix. An injected regression might be that the *labels* order by locale but values don't rotate.\n\nWe tested mapping in en-US where first day = Sunday (no rotation needed). A rotation bug wouldn't show in en-US! To test, I need the Monday-first locale again, select the first chip (M) and check the summary says Monday (not Sunday).\n\nThis is a strong candidate. Let me switch back to English (UK), test chip mapping, then revert. Slightly more work but worth it.\n\nPlan:\n1. Settings → Look and feel → Language → English → United Kingdom.\n2. Back to app, open Pay rent → repeat → custom → week.\n3. In week view, chips M T W T F S S. Tap first chip (M). Tap OK. Check repeat summary: expect \"Repeats weekly on Mon\" not \"Sun\".\n4. Also tap last chip (S) → expect Sun (not Sat) maybe.\n5. Cancel/restore monthly, revert language to System default.\n\nActually, better to test the first chip: if mapping is off by one (labels rotated only), first chip M would produce \"Sun\". Let's do it.\n\nLet me switch language again. This is a bunch of steps but decisive."}
